# Final System - Build Notes

In this stage, we start constructing the LFS system in earnest.

At this point, there should be a toolchain built, either from 
source or upgraded toolchain from a past build. It should be
symlinked to the host's root filesystem:
```
file /tools
```

Should return something like this:
>/tools: symbolic link to /mnt/lfs/tools

make sure the $LFS variable is set
```
echo $LFS
```

Should return something like this:
>/mnt/lfs 

Make sure ther virtual kernel file systems are mounted
```
mount | grep $LFS
```

Should return something like this:
>/dev/sda3 on /mnt/glfs type ext4 (rw,relatime)

>udev on /mnt/glfs/dev type devtmpfs (rw,nosuid,relatime,size=7849156k,nr_inodes=1962289,mode=755,inode64)

>devpts on /mnt/glfs/dev/pts type devpts (rw,relatime,gid=5,mode=620,ptmxmode=000)

>proc on /mnt/glfs/proc type proc (rw,relatime)

>sysfs on /mnt/glfs/sys type sysfs (rw,relatime)

>tmpfs on /mnt/glfs/run type tmpfs (rw,relatime,inode64)

If not, follow "1-Preparation/Build-Toolchain/2-Chroot/03-Prepare_VKS" 
and then return here. 

Enter the chroot environment as root or a super user, 
if not done so already:
```
chroot "$LFS" /tools/bin/env -i   \
    HOME=/root                    \
    TERM="$TERM"                  \
    PS1='(lfs chroot) \u:\w\$ '          \
    PATH=/usr/bin:/usr/sbin:/tools/bin   \
    /tools/bin/bash --login +h
```

